ngl `a ~ Add(b, r)` puts a + b on r
Add(b, r) vs a     => b ~ AddWith[a](r)
AddWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a + b
Sub(b, r) vs a     => b ~ SubWith[a](r)
SubWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a - b
Mul(b, r) vs a     => b ~ MulWith[a](r)
MulWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a * b
Div(b, r) vs a     => b ~ DivWith[a](r)
DivWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a / b
Mod(b, r) vs a     => b ~ ModWith[a](r)
ModWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a % b
Eq(b, r) vs a      => b ~ EqWith[a](r)
EqWith[a](r) vs b  => r ~ a == b
Lt(b, r) vs a      => b ~ LtWith[a](r)
LtWith[a](r) vs b  => r ~ a < b
Gt(b, r) vs a      => b ~ GtWith[a](r)
GtWith[a](r) vs b  => r ~ a > b